description:
Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com

We’re looking for an algorithmic thinking person who is passionate about technology.
We’re looking for a person who is methodical and pays very close attention to details, but who also has the initiative to challenge and improve existing routines and processes. All of the above with respect to the standards of quality, speed and stability Bitdefender proudly promotes.

Responsibilities:

- Develop and maintain services with high availability &high scalability requirements;

- Review requirements and proposed architectures for scalability and reliability issues;

- Collaborate with the Product Owner and Product Manager to correctly understand and clarify requirements, timelines and restrictions;

- Collaborate with and support QA to ensure the quality of software;

Ideally, you should have:

- At least 2 years of experience;

- Strong logical and algorithmic thinking;

- Strong knowledge of JavaScript and NodeJS;

- Knowledge of JavaScript unit testing frameworks;

- Experience with micro service architectures;

- Experience with NoSQL databases like MongoDB, Redis;

- Experience with Agile development environments;

- The ability to work independently;

It would be a plus:

- If you had a bachelor’s degree in Computer Science;

- If you have full stack experience;

- If you have experience building high availability web services.

Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com

About the job

Our mobile security stack is built SDK-first: the protection capabilities that power our consumer and partner apps — secure networking and VPN, web and scam protection, device security — ship as reusable iOS frameworks. We work in a shared, co-versioned codebase consumed by native and Flutter-based apps across the platform, and we are actively embracing the future of software development, including AI-assisted coding, test automation, and intelligent development workflows.

What we're looking for

We are looking for an inquisitive, technology-driven engineer with a strong programming foundation and a genuine interest in building software that other developers depend on. SDK work rewards clean API design, backward-compatibility discipline, and an instinct for what "stable" really means. You should be eager to learn, comfortable solving problems that range from well-defined to open-ended, and motivated to deliver software that meets Bitdefender's standards for quality, performance, and stability.

Ideally, you should have

- 2+ years of software development experience, preferably building for iOS;

- Proficiency in Swift — or strong fundamentals in another language and the ability to ramp up quickly; we value having built real software and being able to read and reason about code over mastery of any single language;

- Fluency with the iOS toolchain — Xcode, Instruments, and the Simulator — and comfort profiling, debugging, and measuring what you ship;

- Experience designing or maintaining reusable components, libraries, or SDKs — clean public APIs, sensible versioning, and an eye for what breaks downstream consumers;

- Solid foundation in algorithms, data structures, and design patterns;

- Comfort with concurrency and synchronization — modern Swift Concurrency (async/await, actors) and/or GCD, and an understanding of the data races they prevent;

- The ability to write unit, integration, and functional tests to ensure code quality and coverage;

- Familiarity with Agile methodologies and version control (Git);

- Strong communication skills and fluency in English.

Bonus points for

- Framework distribution know-how — XCFramework packaging, Swift Package Manager, binary vs. source distribution, and managing dependencies for library consumers;

- Familiarity with iOS internals relevant to security and networking — NetworkExtension, background execution, Keychain, code signing, and entitlements;

- AI-native development — AI coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot) are already part of your workflow, with practical outcomes to show for it. Prompt engineering or agent-based workflows are a strong plus;

- A natural openness to new technologies — you enjoy evaluating, prototyping, and adopting new tools and frameworks when they earn their place;

- A Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field;

- A portfolio of past projects (e.g. GitHub, Bitbucket, or similar).

What you'll do

- Contribute to the design, development, and evolution of Bitdefender's iOS security SDKs and the components that power them — owning features end to end, from public API to tests;

- Care for the contract you expose: stable APIs, clean versioning, and changes that don't surprise the apps that depend on you;

- Write and maintain unit, integration, and functional tests to ensure robust coverage and long-term code health;

- Apply AI-assisted development workflows in your daily practice — using tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or GitHub Copilot for code generation, test scaffolding, and review acceleration;

- Collaborate with Product Owners, QA engineers, and other developers in an Agile Scrum environment;

- Continuously evaluate and adopt new tools, frameworks, and technologies to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of our development process.

#LI-BM1

Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com

About the role

We are recruiting a Senior Legal Advisor who will work in the areas of Corporate, Mergers and Acquisitions (M&A) and Employment Law at the Bitdefender Group level. The role is not limited to the application of Romanian law (nevertheless we do not expect the candidate to have expertise in other jurisdictions): the candidate will participate in multinational projects and supervise the work of external lawyers from the relevant jurisdictions. The candidate is expected to advise on complex topics, participate in large-scale legal projects, and be responsible for the organization's compliance with the applicable legal framework in the jurisdictions in which we operate in collaboration with the local lawyers.

Main responsibilities

Corporate Law and Corporate Governance

- Provide legal advice on the functioning of the group companies;

- Prepare and review corporate documents (resolutions of the General Shareholders' Meeting, decisions of the management bodies, articles of incorporation, amendments to the articles of association etc.);

- Support the implementation of corporate governance best practices and ensure compliance with statutory and reporting obligations.

- Manage the KYC process within the Group

- Manage the compliance with different laws and directives at the Group level.

Mergers and Acquisitions (M&A)

- Coordinate and participate in legal due diligence processes for acquisition, merger, division or reorganization operations;

- Drafts and negotiates the specific documentation of the transactions (term sheet, SPA, contracts for the assignment of shares/shares, confidentiality agreements, declarations and guarantees etc.);

- Manage post-transaction integration aspects and, where applicable, competition notifications and authorizations, facility agreements;

- Collaborate with external advisors, financial and tax teams throughout the entire transaction cycle.

Labour law

- Provide advice on all aspects of the employment relationship;

- Drafting and reviewing individual employment contracts, addenda, job descriptions, internal regulations and internal policies;

- Coordinate the procedures for termination of employment contracts, dismissals, disciplinary procedures and disciplinary investigations;

Generals

- Ensure the general legal compliance of the activity and the implementation of internal procedures;

- Coordinate and supervise the work of external lawyers and consultants in the relevant jurisdictions;

- Participate in multinational legal projects and support business and management teams through pragmatic legal advice, oriented towards the organization's objectives.

Requirements

- Bachelor's degree in Law; Master's degrees or relevant specializations in corporate law/M&A/labor law are an advantage;

- Minimum 10 years of relevant experience, acquired within large or medium-large companies with complex corporate structure and international exposure (corporate environment – e.g. IT&C, energy, retail, manufacturing, services, technology), either in in-house legal departments or in law firms/firms;

- Solid and demonstrable experience in corporate law, M&A transactions and employment law;

- Very good knowledge of the applicable Romanian legal framework (Law no. 31/1990, Labor Code, legislation on competition and M&A transactions) and ability to coordinate multinational projects and supervise external consultants from other jurisdictions;

- Excellent communication skills in English (advanced level);

- Ability to manage complex and multiple legal projects in parallel, with high autonomy and responsibility;

- Strategic thinking, attention to detail, organized spirit, flexibility and ability to collaborate in a multicultural environment;

Offer and benefits

- Senior role, with visibility and direct impact on the organization's strategic decisions;

- Involvement in large-scale transactions and legal projects, in a dynamic corporate environment;

- Opportunities for continuous professional development and collaboration with multidisciplinary teams, locally and internationally.

Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com

About the role
We are recruiting a Legal Advisor who will work in the areas of Commercial Law, Compliance, IT Law and Intellectual Property (IP) for Bitdefender Group companies worldwide. The role is not limited to the application of Romanian law (nevertheless we do not expect the candidate to have expertise in other jurisdictions): the candidate will supervise commercial agreements, license agreements and any legal related matters, ensuring that the organization meets all legal requirements in its operations. The candidate is expected to advise business and technical teams on complex topics, participate in multinational projects and collaborate with external lawyers from the relevant jurisdictions.

Main responsibilities
Commercial Law and Compliance

- Prepare and review all contracts with clients and suppliers to ensure compliance with applicable laws and internal procedures;

- Ensure compliance with all relevant legal requirements across the organization's operations;

- Ensure that tasks related to the organization's legal affairs are completed in an efficient and economical manner in order to contribute to the achievement of the organization's goals;

- Follow up on all legal cases with external legal advisors and local courts.

IT, Communications and Data Privacy

- Ensure compliance with IT, communications and privacy laws and handle these matters within the Bitdefender group of companies;

- Advise on regulatory developments in the areas of data protection, cybersecurity and telecommunications legislation;

- Support the implementation of internal policies and procedures in line with the applicable legal framework.

Intellectual Property (IP)

- Advise on IP-related matters, including the protection and management of trademarks, copyrights and other intellectual property rights;

- Prepare and review license agreements and IP-related contractual documentation.

Mergers & Acquisitions (M&A) Support

- Offer support in due diligence processes for M&A activities of the Bitdefender group of companies;

- Collaborate with internal and external teams throughout the transaction cycle.

Generals

- Serve as an advisor to business and technical teams and maintain relationships within the Bitdefender group of companies;

- Coordinate and supervise the work of external lawyers and consultants in the relevant jurisdictions;

- Participate in multinational legal projects and support business and management teams through pragmatic legal advice, oriented towards the organization's objectives.

Requirements

- Bachelor's degree in Law;

- Minimum 7 years of relevant experience, acquired within the Legal Department of a large IT or communications company, either in in-house legal departments or in law firms;

- Solid and demonstrable knowledge of commercial, IP and IT laws;

- Very good knowledge of the applicable Romanian legal framework and ability to coordinate multinational projects and supervise external consultants from other jurisdictions;

- Excellent communication skills in English (advanced level);

- French or German communication skills are a plus;

- Highly responsible and motivated to work within a multicultural environment;

- Attention to detail, organized spirit, flexibility and ability to manage multiple projects in parallel.

Offer and benefits

- Involvement in diverse legal projects across commercial, compliance, IT and IP law, in a dynamic corporate environment;

- Opportunities for continuous professional development and collaboration with multidisciplinary teams, locally and internationally;

- Collaboration with business and technical teams within a leading global cybersecurity company.

#LI-SA1

Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com

Our mobile security stack is built SDK-first: the protection capabilities that power our consumer and partner apps (secure networking and VPN, web and scam protection, device security) ship as reusable Android libraries. We work in a shared, co-versioned codebase consumed by native and Flutter-based apps across the platform, and we are actively embracing the future of software development, including AI-assisted coding, test automation, and intelligent development workflows.

What We’re Looking For

We are looking for an inquisitive, technology-driven engineer with a strong programming foundation and a genuine interest in building software that other developers depend on. SDK work rewards clean API design, backward-compatibility discipline, and an instinct for what “stable” really means. You should be eager to learn, comfortable solving problems that range from well-defined to open-ended, and motivated to deliver software that meets Bitdefender’s standards for quality, performance, and stability.

Ideally, You Should Have

- 2+ years of software development experience, preferably building for Android;

- Proficiency in Kotlin, or strong fundamentals in another language (Java counts) and the ability to ramp up quickly; we value having built real software and being able to read and reason about code over mastery of any single language;

- Fluency with the Android toolchain (Android Studio, Gradle, the Android Profiler, Logcat and the Emulator) and comfort profiling, debugging, and measuring what you ship;

- Experience designing or maintaining reusable components, libraries, or SDKs: clean public APIs, sensible versioning, and an eye for what breaks downstream consumers;

- Solid foundation in algorithms, data structures, and design patterns;

- Comfort with concurrency and synchronization: Kotlin Coroutines and Flow (structured concurrency, dispatchers, cancellation) and/or Java threading primitives, and an understanding of the race conditions they prevent;

- The ability to write unit, integration, and instrumented tests (e.g. JUnit, MockK, Espresso) to ensure code quality and coverage;

- Familiarity with Agile methodologies and version control (Git);

- Strong communication skills and fluency in English.

Bonus Points For

- Library distribution know-how: AAR packaging, publishing to Maven repositories, Gradle build logic and convention plugins, and managing transitive dependencies for library consumers;

- Familiarity with Android internals relevant to security and networking: VpnService, foreground services and background execution limits, WorkManager, Android Keystore, runtime permissions, app signing, and behaviour differences across OS versions and OEMs;

- AI-native development: AI coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot) are already part of your workflow, with practical outcomes to show for it. Prompt engineering or agent-based workflows are a strong plus;

- A natural openness to new technologies: you enjoy evaluating, prototyping, and adopting new tools and frameworks when they earn their place;

- A Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field;

- A portfolio of past projects (e.g. GitHub, Bitbucket, or similar).

What You’ll Do

- Contribute to the design, development, and evolution of Bitdefender’s Android security SDKs and the components that power them, owning features end to end, from public API to tests;

- Care for the contract you expose: stable APIs, clean versioning, and changes that don’t surprise the apps that depend on you;

- Write and maintain unit, integration, and instrumented tests to ensure robust coverage and long-term code health;

- Apply AI-assisted development workflows in your daily practice, using tools like Claude Code, Cursor, or GitHub Copilot for code generation, test scaffolding, and review acceleration;

- Collaborate with Product Owners, UX designers, QA engineers, and other developers in an Agile Scrum environment;

- Continuously evaluate and adopt new tools, frameworks, and technologies to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of our development process.

What We Offer

- A dynamic and exciting work environment in a leading cybersecurity company;

- Competitive benefits aligned with your performance and contribution;

- Opportunities for professional growth and involvement in cutting-edge projects

