Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com

We are seeking dedicated specialists determined to build a successful career in Software Quality Assurance. Bitdefender values its Quality Assurance teams as professionals performing critical functions in the software development lifecycle and appreciates their decisive contribution to the success of our products.

Requirements
We're looking for a well-organised person who is passionate about technology. The ideal candidate should have:
- A bachelor's degree in Computer Science;
- 3+ years of experience as a QA engineer for full-stack applications in an Agile development environment;
- Strong QA skills (troubleshooting, bug isolation and reporting, good understanding of testing concepts, methodologies and processes);
- Experience testing web applications, backend services, and APIs;
- Knowledge of QA automation architecture, methodologies, processes, and tools;
- 1+ years' experience in test automation;
- Working experience with web end-to-end testing/automation frameworks like Playwright or similar;
- Experience automating functional and integration testing;
- Experience in any programming language;
- Curiosity about, or prior exposure to, testing AI-powered features or LLM-based applications (e.g. evaluating model outputs, prompt/response validation, agentic workflows) is a strong plus;
- Ability to work in an energising environment with rapidly changing requirements;
- Excellent analytical skills and ability to autonomously solve problems, as well as collaborate with direct and extended teams;
- Strong verbal and written communication skills.

It will be a plus:
- ISTQB Foundation or any other QA certification;
- Familiarity with testing approaches for non-deterministic systems (e.g. LLM output evaluation, regression testing for AI agents, hallucination/edge-case detection).

Job Responsibilities
You will have the opportunity to contribute to the development and delivery of Bitdefender's next-generation products, including applied AI and agent-based capabilities. You will be responsible for:
- Developing, maintaining, documenting, and executing test plans for Bitdefender products, including AI-driven and agentic features;
- Reporting issues through the bug tracking system, effectively following up and communicating test results;
- Performing tests against builds and test procedures;
- Conducting root-cause analysis and tracking defect resolution to completion;
- Researching, recommending, and implementing tools as needed to improve the testing process, product quality, and test automation coverage;
- Designing, implementing, and executing automated test suites;
- Contributing to test strategies for LLM-based and agentic product components, including validating behavior consistency, response quality, and edge-case handling where applicable.
- All of this with respect to the standards of quality and stability Bitdefender proudly promotes.
- You will work in an Agile Scrum environment, interacting with the Product Owner, Scrum Master, software developers, UX designers, and other QA engineers.

Job Offer
If you take up our offer, you will:
- Work in a fast-moving environment at the intersection of cybersecurity and applied AI, with exposure to next-generation product development;
- Have the opportunity to grow into specialized automation or AI-testing tracks as our product portfolio expands;
- Enjoy benefits scaled to your performance, along with a competitive salary, medical and accident insurance;
- Be part of a collaborative QA team with strong mentorship and room for professional development, including support for certifications.

#LI-AI1

Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com

The Renewal & Retention representative is responsible for achieving quarterly and annual goals by managing a territory using the telephone and Web 2.0 technologies mainly.

The Renewal & Retention Representative acts as Account Responsible for allocated accounts and will follow two main objectives: on one hand work closely with Bitdefender’s channel partners to retain customers, secure and maximize the revenue on existing allocated accounts; on the other hand, the representative will build direct relationships with end-users in order to help them take full advantage of their investment and continue their engagement with Bitdefender.

Responsibilities:

- Renewals in the allocated segment achieved through business partners or direct contact with end-users:

- Meets assigned renewal related targets and strategic objectives in the agreed territory/segment/threshold;

- Proactively and timely manages the renewal pipeline by engaging with Bitdefender’s channel partners and end users;

- Accurately documents and updates the CRM with relevant information about the renewal and customer satisfaction level;

- Responsible for forecasting revenue renewal projections and participates in forecast meetings with management and other stakeholders;

- Actively seeks to maximize renewal revenue through upsell/upgrade/cross-sell actions;

- Promotes marketing upselling & retention campaigns to drive revenue growth and increase Customer Retention;

- Leads solution development efforts that best address end-user needs, while coordinating the involvement of all necessary Bitdefender resources and partner personnel;

- Ability to develop territory growth plans in collaboration with TAM, ITAM and CAM

Proactive and programmatic retention activities:

- Uses tele sales and customer engagement techniques for interacting with end users to increase their level of engagement with Bitdefender’s products & services, throughout the Customer Lifecycle Stages;

- Conducts customer outreach over the phone with weekly monitoring of call rates, time on the phone and activity levels;

- Closely follows the cadence set for end-user engagement/churn prevention throughout the fiscal year in line with agreed customer contact strategy & objectives while using appropriate channels;

- Accurately assess a customer’s level of churn risk and/or down sell based on customer’s feedback and by using various digital assessment tools and reports;

- Uses people and technology resources appropriately to proactively address and correct identified risks for assigned accounts;

- Makes recommendations to help at-risk customers, promote overall customer satisfaction, product adoption, retention, and renewals;

- Partners with Sales (Sales teams, Partner Ecosystem, Technical Support, Sales Support, Etc.) on account and territory planning as appropriate to promote a positive customer experience;

- Meets assigned renewal and retention targets and aligns themselves with the regional strategy set by the Regional Director/TAM/ITAM/CAM leaders;

Qualifications:

- French - Full professional proficiency;

- English - Full professional proficiency;

- Bachelor’s Degree;

- 1+ years of Customer success, renewals, and or inside-sales experience and an understanding of a 2 tier distribution model is a plus;

- Extensive experience in Customer Success is a plus;

- Negotiation, B2B, and closing skills;

- Must have a proven track record of success in achieving measurable monthly lead development/sales goals;

- Strong time management and organizational skills. Able to manage and meet multiple deadlines;

- Positive and energetic phone skills, excellent listening skills, strong written communication skills;

- Strong interpersonal skills suitable for interacting with various departments, system personnel, all levels of management, and customers in the surrounding community;

- Knowledge of Salesforce CRM software and Microsoft Office preferred;

- Adaptive and flexible (changing technologies, processes, etc);

- Travel to territory on an as needed basis.

#LI-SA1

Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com

Job Description
We are looking for an experienced QA professional to take a senior role within our Software Quality Assurance teams. At Bitdefender, QA teams play a critical role throughout the software development lifecycle, and we highly value their contribution to the quality and success of our products. As a Senior QA Engineer, you will act as a technical reference point for the team, drive automation and quality standards, and mentor colleagues while owning the testing of critical product areas.

Responsibilities
As a Senior QA Engineer, your responsibilities will include:

- Developing, maintaining, documenting, and executing comprehensive test plans, test cases, and test suites for the Bitdefender macOS product suite;

- Analyzing design and project specifications early to prevent defects, identify gaps in documentation, and design broad test scenarios before implementation begins;

- Performing both manual and automated testing activities — functional, regression, integration, system, load, stress, security, and performance;

- Designing, implementing, and maintaining complex automated test scripts and contributing to the development and upkeep of the team's automation platforms, with a strong focus on expanding coverage and improving efficiency;

- Reporting issues through the bug tracking system, conducting root cause analysis, and following defects through to resolution, including validating fixes and assessing the impact of code changes;

- Producing manual and automated test run reports and communicating results, status, and quality metrics to the release owner to support go/no-go decisions;

- Owning and monitoring quality metrics and indicators within your area of responsibility, and participating in risk analysis for product and module functionalities;

- Researching, recommending, and implementing tools and approaches that improve the testing process, product quality, and overall automation level;

- Using modern AI-based tools to improve testing efficiency, test design, analysis, and automation workflows, while applying sound judgment to validate results;

- Mentoring and helping train Junior QA Engineers — supporting them in clarifying specifications, reporting and reproducing defects, and growing their technical skills;

- Sharing technical knowledge across teams and delivering clear documentation and workshops in your area of expertise;

- Contributing to the technical evaluation of team members' performance and to the assessment of candidates' technical competencies for open positions, in line with company procedures;

- Identifying training needs and organizing sessions to raise the overall quality standard of testing;

- Reproducing and investigating errors reported by customers, collaborating with Technical Support and the Cyber Threat Intelligence Lab to identify root causes;

- Ensuring that the product meets all target requirements and quality standards before each release.

Requirements

- 4+ years of experience as a QA Engineer in the software domain;

- Experience with macOS or Linux;

- Strong scripting skills, preferably in Python or Bash, and solid hands-on experience in QA automation;

- Proven ability to test critical areas and modules, and to prioritize testing based on risk;

- Solid QA skills, including troubleshooting, bug isolation and reporting, and a strong understanding of testing concepts, methodologies, and processes;

- Experience with test case management tools, bug tracking tools, and Git;

- Solid experience with analysis tools — metrics, charts, and quality indicators;

- Experience creating and executing security and performance tests;

- Openness to using AI tools in day-to-day work, with a practical mindset and the ability to critically assess the results;

- Strong critical thinking and analytical skills — testing starts with the first requirements and continues throughout development;

- Very good attention to detail and a meticulous approach to quality;

- Basic to intermediate networking knowledge, and a good understanding of the technology and architecture behind the products;

- Ability to mentor and support junior colleagues, with good teaching and communication skills;

- ISTQB Foundation certification (or equivalent) is a plus;

- A bachelor’s degree in computer science is a plus;

- Good written and spoken English skills;

- A collaborative and enthusiastic team player with a strong willingness to learn and continuously improve;

- Commitment to the standards of quality and stability that Bitdefender proudly promotes;

- Ability to work in an Agile Scrum environment, collaborating with the Product Owner, Scrum Master, software developers, UX designers, and fellow QA engineers.

Job Offer
If you join us, you will:

- Work on great technologies and products;

- Be part of one of Bitdefender's best QA teams;

- Enjoy a flexible work schedule;

- Benefit from career development programs.
